= Pool 1

# Start
- Send Activity
- Send Event
. Send End Event

= Pool 2

.# Start
// You can add the `~receive` attribute to make it look nicer.
.- Receive Activity ~receive
// If you use the long form of events, you need to use the message event.
M# Receive Event
.. End Event (cannot receive messages)


// Recommendation: Keep message flows at the end after sequence flows and after data.
// Message flows can have a label, written at the very end (similar to boundary events)
MF <-send-activity ->receive-activity Message Flow Label
// Nodes can have multiple incoming or outgoing message flows.
MF <-send-event ->receive-activity
MF <-send-end-event ->receive-event

// Note: Message flows between two `~blackbox` pools are not shown.
